```csharp
private void SetInstalledTileSizeVisibility(bool tiles)
{
    var vis = tiles ? Visibility.Visible : Visibility.Collapsed;
    InstalledTileSizeLabel.Visibility = vis;
}
```

Wait, but I'm calling this correctly with `tiles` as the parameter. Let me fix my implementation - `SetInstalledTileSizeVisibility(tiles)` should show both label and slider when `tiles` is true. My current code has an extra `Visible(false)` for Installed but that looks wrong - let me re-read.

```csharp
private void SetInstalledTileSizeVisibility(bool visible)
{
    InstalledTileSizeLabel.Visibility = Visible(true);   // This shows it regardless of 'visible' parameter!
    InstalledTileSizeSlider.Visibility = Visible(false);  // Always collapsed
}
```

This is clearly wrong. The `Visible(true)` ignores the `visible` parameter. Let me fix this properly:

